REVERSA – third-party licenses
==============================

REVERSA (MIT) is written in C++. To build and run, it uses only the third-party
components below. CI checks that this list is complete with tools/check_licenses.cpp
(every dependency from CMakeLists.txt and vcpkg.json must be listed here and have an
allowed license).

Part of the program
-------------------

1. Capstone
   Version: 5.0.9 (CMake FetchContent, pinned git tag)
   License: BSD-3-Clause
   Copyright (c) 2013, COSEINC; Nguyen Anh Quynh and contributors
   Source: https://github.com/capstone-engine/capstone
   Use: disassembler, linked statically without changes.
   Obligation: keep the copyright and license text when redistributing.

2. SQLite
   License: public domain
   Source: https://sqlite.org (Linux: system package libsqlite3, Windows: vcpkg, version
   locked by builtin-baseline in vcpkg.json)
   Use: the .rvproj project format.

3. Qt 6 (QtCore, QtGui, QtWidgets)
   License: LGPL-3.0-only
   Source: https://www.qt.io, https://code.qt.io
   Use: graphical interface. Qt is linked dynamically and shipped as separate,
   replaceable libraries (Windows: Qt6*.dll next to reversa.exe, Linux: system
   packages). Users can replace Qt with their own build, which meets the LGPL
   conditions. The Qt source code is available at code.qt.io. Qt is not modified.

Development tools
-----------------
Tests and repository checks (tools/*.cpp, tests/cpp) use only the C++ standard library
and the components above. No other third-party tools are downloaded.

Inspiration (no code copied)
----------------------------
We studied design patterns and algorithms in Ghidra (Apache-2.0), radare2 (LGPL-3.0),
rizin/Cutter (LGPL-3.0/GPL-3.0), angr (BSD-2-Clause), RetDec (MIT), LIEF (Apache-2.0),
Detect It Easy (MIT) and binwalk (MIT). No source code was copied from these
projects; see docs/research.md.

Test samples
------------
samples/bin/* are compiled from our own sources samples/src/*.c (MIT) by
samples/build.sh. They contain startup code of runtime libraries (glibc,
MinGW-w64 CRT), which is under licenses with a runtime exception
(LGPL-2.1 + exception / GCC Runtime Library Exception / ZPL / public domain).
